lines+=['Full NBA/WNBA tables are in outcome-tables.csv and outcome-tables.json.','','5. Trailing-team tests','Eight injected NBA endings, 80 paired seeds per arm, five arms (3,200 final test cases). Synthetic starting score and clock; these are not full-game or league-frequency estimates. Half the seed configurations reduce three-point ability equally in both arms.','Foul arm: extends the intentional-foul window to 55 seconds when down 4–6; permits another prompt intentional foul after a foul-to-give rather than immediately resuming a long setup. The existing bonus, player foul and FT mechanics resolve it.','Quick-two arm: when down two within 30 seconds, weights inside opportunities ×1.3 and three-point opportunities ×.7; it does not force a two or change accuracy.','Timeout arm: at eligible acquisition before advancing the ball, uses an available timeout and reduces setup to at most one second. At most two added advancement timeouts per team and the existing four-timeout budget. This is a timing approximation: the engine lacks explicit backcourt/frontcourt coordinates and a complete NBA mandatory-timeout inventory. It is not a fully verified advance-the-ball implementation and is NOT promoted.','Combined arm tests these together. All late-game arms remain experimental; their results must not be represented as a full-season OT improvement.','Case | N/arm | Baseline final wins / OT | Combined final wins / OT']
